{"type":"message","id":"f0f934b0","parentId":"43d15acf","timestamp":"2026-03-15T07:00:00.134Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:0bd24b87-4e9d-4cf4-8005-b21e45f87aca conversation-review] You are a memory consolidation agent. Your job is to review today's conversations and extract important information worth saving.\n\n## Your Task\n\n1. First, read the session history to find all conversations from today (2026-03-01). Look in:\n   - Discord channels (check message history)\n   - Any TUI sessions\n\n2. Extract anything worth remembering:\n   - Decisions made\n   - Preferences stated\n   - Facts about Noah\n   - Tasks completed or assigned\n   - Plans discussed\n   - Ideas generated\n   - Anything explicitly asked to remember\n   - Anything important that should be saved\n\n3. For each item extracted:\n   - Check if it already exists in ~/workspace/MEMORY.md or ~/workspace/memory/2026-03-01.md\n   - If new, write durable facts to ~/workspace/MEMORY.md\n   - Write daily context to ~/workspace/memory/2026-03-01.md\n   - File relevant content to appropriate ~/obsidian-vault/ folder:\n     - Fitness/health → projects/personal-trainer/\n     - Food/recipes → projects/personal-chef/\n     - Productivity/time-blocking → projects/time-blocking/\n     - Research/links → references/\n     - Daily logs → daily/2026-03-01.md\n   - Use clear filenames (e.g., \"leg-day-routine.md\", not \"notes.md\")\n   - Do NOT duplicate - update existing entries if something changed\n\n4. After writing everything, git commit and push the obsidian vault:\n   ```bash\n   cd ~/obsidian-vault\n   git add -A\n   git commit -m \"Memory update: $(date +%Y-%m-%d)\"\n   git push\n   ```\n\n5. Post a summary to the channel you were triggered from (or #general-chat if unknown). Format:\n   - \"📝 Saved X new items to memory\"\n   - \"📂 Updated Y vault files\"\n   - List each item on one line\n   - If nothing worth saving, post \"nothing new today\"\n\n## Important\n- Be thorough - check ALL channels\n- Don't fabricate entries - only save real information\n- Before writing, check if info already exists\n- Update existing files rather than creating duplicates\nCurrent time: Sunday, March 15th, 2026 — 7:00 AM (UTC) / 2026-03-15 07:00 UTC\n\nReturn your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically. If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself."}],"timestamp":1773558000131}}
